WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:15.364
The next day a strange thing happened in the attic.

2
00:00:17.065 --> 00:00:19.307
Sara was out doing errands as usual.

3
00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:25.592
So Mel the rat was the only one who saw and heard what happened.

4
00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:29.994
Mel had left his hole and was looking for food in Sara's room.

5
00:00:32.095 --> 00:00:34.216
Suddenly he heard a noise on the roof.

6
00:00:36.898 --> 00:00:40.099
Two men opened the skylight and then peered through it.

7
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.562
One man was Ram Dass, the Indian servant from next door.

8
00:00:45.422 --> 00:00:47.663
The other was a young man—Mr.

9
00:00:47.723 --> 00:00:49.104
Carrisford's secretary.

10
00:00:50.885 --> 00:00:53.947
Mel watched the two men enter the room through the skylight.

11
00:00:55.027 --> 00:00:56.268
Neither one made a sound.

12
00:00:58.584 --> 00:01:02.567
Mel was used to Sara by now, but the two strangers frightened him.

13
00:01:03.687 --> 00:01:06.929
He ran into his hole, but he kept an eye on the two men.

14
00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:10.651
The secretary had caught a glimpse of Mel's tail.

15
00:01:10.671 --> 00:01:12.853
"Was that a rat?"

16
00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:15.034
he whispered to Ram Dass.

17
00:01:15.054 --> 00:01:18.296
"Yes," Ram Dass whispered back.

18
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:21.578
"There are many rats living in these walls."

19
00:01:21.598 --> 00:01:25.100
"Ugh!" exclaimed the young man.

20
00:01:25.872 --> 00:01:28.594
"I'm surprised the girl is not terrified by them."

21
00:01:29.975 --> 00:01:32.958
"She's not like other children," replied Ram Dass.

22
00:01:33.758 --> 00:01:35.600
"She's a friend to all living creatures.

23
00:01:36.861 --> 00:01:40.164
I often watch her from my skylight and see her talking to the birds.

24
00:01:41.665 --> 00:01:44.727
She's kind to humans too," Ram Dass went on.

25
00:01:44.747 --> 00:01:48.911
"The servant girl in the next room comes to her for comfort.

26
00:01:50.111 --> 00:01:52.714
Then there is a blond girl who comes to hear her stories.

27
00:01:53.915 --> 00:01:55.536
And a little girl who worships her.

28
00:01:56.992 --> 00:01:59.414
The mistress of the house treats her like an outcast.

29
00:02:00.094 --> 00:02:02.996
But the girl acts like she comes from a family of kings.

30
00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.398
She's a true princess!"

31
00:02:05.418 --> 00:02:10.421
"You seem to know a lot about her," the secretary said.

32
00:02:11.362 --> 00:02:12.343
Ram Dass nodded.

33
00:02:12.363 --> 00:02:15.044
"I watch her closely," he said.

34
00:02:15.064 --> 00:02:18.066
"Are you sure she won't come up here now?"

35
00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:19.828
the secretary asked.

36
00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:22.630
"If she finds us, she'll be frightened.

37
00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:24.791
And it would spoil Mr.

38
00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:25.912
Carrisford's plans."

39
00:02:26.848 --> 00:02:30.911
"She has gone out and probably won't return for hours," said Ram Dass.

40
00:02:30.931 --> 00:02:35.694
"Besides, I can hear anyone on the stairs.

41
00:02:36.815 --> 00:02:38.737
We'll have time to escape if necessary."

42
00:02:39.777 --> 00:02:42.639
The secretary took a pencil and paper from his pocket.

43
00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:44.741
"Keep your ears open."

44
00:02:47.403 --> 00:02:51.846
He began to walk slowly around the miserable little room, making notes.

45
00:02:52.867 --> 00:02:54.368
First he went to the narrow bed.

46
00:02:55.028 --> 00:02:56.770
He pressed his hand on the mattress.

47
00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.072
"Hard as a rock!"

48
00:02:59.572 --> 00:03:00.433
he exclaimed.

49
00:03:00.453 --> 00:03:04.076
"The blanket is thin and the sheets are ragged."

50
00:03:05.598 --> 00:03:07.660
Then he looked at the dark fireplace.

51
00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.522
"There hasn't been a fire there for days."

52
00:03:10.542 --> 00:03:15.246
"I've never seen a fire there," said Ram Dass.

53
00:03:15.266 --> 00:03:17.508
"It's always freezing in here.

54
00:03:18.409 --> 00:03:21.132
I don't believe the mistress cares how cold the girl gets."

55
00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.182
"What a place for a child to sleep in!"

56
00:03:25.642 --> 00:03:26.663
said the secretary.

57
00:03:27.904 --> 00:03:30.506
He noted the old table and bare floor.

58
00:03:32.147 --> 00:03:33.708
"Whose idea was it to help her?"

59
00:03:33.728 --> 00:03:36.850
"It was mine," said Ram Dass.

60
00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:40.213
"I like to hear the stories she tells her friends.

61
00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:45.497
One night she pretended this room was warm, comfortable, and filled with beautiful things."

62
00:03:46.657 --> 00:03:48.939
Ram Dass had repeated Sara's story to Mr.

63
00:03:50.444 --> 00:03:54.006
Carrisford. The sick gentleman had not liked the way she was treated at the school.

64
00:03:55.227 --> 00:03:57.868
He began to think about making her dreams come true.

65
00:03:59.329 --> 00:04:01.970
"Do you think we can transform this room while she sleeps?"

66
00:04:02.571 --> 00:04:03.751
the secretary asked.

67
00:04:03.771 --> 00:04:07.313
"Of course we'd have to replace her bed during the day."

68
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:12.636
"I can do it all with the help of another servant," Ram Dass replied.

69
00:04:12.656 --> 00:04:15.938
"We'll be so quiet that she won't wake up.

70
00:04:16.898 --> 00:04:19.920
When she does awake, she will think that a magician has been here!"

71
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.542
The secretary continued looking around.

72
00:04:24.843 --> 00:04:30.067
He made notes about the floor, the fireplace, the broken footstool, and the old table.

73
00:04:32.109 --> 00:04:35.912
He also remarked that a number of old nails had been placed in the walls.

74
00:04:37.854 --> 00:04:39.595
Ram Dass smiled mysteriously.

75
00:04:39.615 --> 00:04:44.919
"Yesterday when she was out, I entered the room, bringing with me some sharp nails.

76
00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.922
I pressed them into the walls, where we will need them."

77
00:04:49.023 --> 00:04:50.144
The secretary nodded.

78
00:04:50.816 --> 00:04:53.057
"You can hang things on them," he said.

79
00:04:54.238 --> 00:04:55.559
Soon the men were finished.

80
00:04:55.579 --> 00:04:58.041
"I think I've made enough notes.

81
00:04:58.841 --> 00:05:00.982
We can go now," said the secretary.

82
00:05:01.002 --> 00:05:03.064
"It's a shame Mr.

83
00:05:03.084 --> 00:05:05.465
Carrisford has not found that lost child.

84
00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:07.847
He has such a warm heart."

85
00:05:07.867 --> 00:05:11.409
"If he finds her, his strength will return.

86
00:05:12.569 --> 00:05:14.751
He will be well again," said Ram Dass.

87
00:05:14.771 --> 00:05:16.432
"I'm sure of that."

88
00:05:18.208 --> 00:05:22.051
Then the two men slipped silently through the skylight and across the roof.

89
00:05:24.053 --> 00:05:27.115
After Mel was sure they had gone, he came out of his hole.

90
00:05:28.616 --> 00:05:29.877
He sniffed around the floor.

91
00:05:31.058 --> 00:05:33.260
He didn't understand what the men had talked about.

92
00:05:34.321 --> 00:05:36.242
But he hoped they had dropped some crumbs.
